    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Valderrivas area grew on land once occupied by a cement factory that operated from 1923 to 1995.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vic%C3%A1lvaro"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1990s a second center, Valdebernardo, was built just west of Vicálvaro’s historic core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vic%C3%A1lvaro"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1990s saw Line 9 of Metro Madrid extend from Pavones to Arganda del Rey, requiring a transfer at Puerta de Arganda.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vic%C3%A1lvaro"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "New stations like Valdebernardo, Vicálvaro, San Cipriano and Puerta de Arganda feature brightly coloured walls to help passengers avoid missing stops.",
